1          /************************************************************************************************
2           USING THE BY GROUPFORMAT STATEMENT TO PROCESS DATA
                                                           The SAS System

3               This program creates a format that can be used to group data. It shows the use of the groupformat option in the data
3        !  step.
4               Keywords: PROC FORMAT, FORMAT, VALUE, GROUPFORMAT
5               SAS Versions: SAS 9, SAS Viya
6               Documentation:
6        ! https://documentation.sas.com/?cdcId=pgmsascdc&cdcVersion=default&docsetId=proc&docsetTarget=p1xidhqypi0fnwn1if8opjpqpbmn
6        ! .htm
7               1. Create a data set on which to test the new format. The data is sorted by the value to be formatted.
8               2. Use PROC FORMAT with a value statement. Provide ranges for which you want to assign different grouping levels.
9               3. Use the groupformat option on the by statement to allow the data step to read the data by groups.
10              4. Because the data is being read with a by statement the first. and last. variables are created. In this example,
10       ! the
11                 first.salary will be the lowest salary observation for a group and the last.salary observation will be the
11       ! highest.
12              5. In the PROC REPORT apply the format to see the results.
13         ************************************************************************************************/
14         data payroll; /*1*/
15            infile cards;
16            input EmployeeID Salary BirthDate : date9. HireDate : date9.;
17            cards;

NOTE: The data set WORK.PAYROLL has 45 observations and 4 variables.
NOTE: DATA statement used (Total process time):
      real time           0.01 seconds
      user cpu time       0.00 seconds
      system cpu time     0.00 seconds
      memory              731.25k
      OS Memory           10068.00k
      Timestamp           10/27/2026 10:55:51 AM
      Step Count                        2  Switch Count  0
      

63         ;
64         run;
65         
66         proc format;
66       !              /*2*/
67            value salgrp low-<30000='Under $30,000'
68                         30000-<35000='$30,000 to $35,000'
69         				35000-<50000='$35,000 to $50,000'
70         				50000-high='Over $50,000';
NOTE: Format SALGRP has been output.
71         run;

NOTE: PROCEDURE FORMAT used (Total process time):
      real time           0.04 seconds
      user cpu time       0.00 seconds
      system cpu time     0.00 seconds
      memory              154.84k
      OS Memory           10068.00k
      Timestamp           10/27/2026 10:55:51 AM
      Step Count                        3  Switch Count  0
      

72         
73         data highlowsal;
74            set payroll;
75            by groupformat salary; /*3*/
                                                           The SAS System

76            format salary salgrp.;
77            if first.salary then output; /*4*/
78            if last.salary then output;
79         run;

NOTE: There were 45 observations read from the data set WORK.PAYROLL.
NOTE: The data set WORK.HIGHLOWSAL has 8 observations and 4 variables.
NOTE: DATA statement used (Total process time):
      real time           0.03 seconds
      user cpu time       0.00 seconds
      system cpu time     0.00 seconds
      memory              907.28k
      OS Memory           10584.00k
      Timestamp           10/27/2026 10:55:51 AM
      Step Count                        4  Switch Count  0
      

80         
81         proc report data=highlowsal nowd; /*5*/
82            columns EmployeeID Salary Salary=SalGrp HireDate;
83            define salary / display format=dollar12.;
84            define hiredate / format=date9.;
85            define salgrp / format=salgrp. 'Salary Group';
86            title 'Lowest and Highest Salary by Salary Group';
87         run;

