1          /*** HEADER
2          
3              Display:     Figure 7.1 Box plot - Measurements by Analysis Timepoint, Visit and Treatment
4              White paper: Central Tendency
5          
6              User Guide:     https://github.com/phuse-org/phuse-scripts/blob/master/whitepapers/CentralTendency-UserGuide.txt
7              Macro Library:  https://github.com/phuse-org/phuse-scripts/tree/master/whitepapers/utilities
8              Specs:          https://github.com/phuse-org/phuse-scripts/tree/master/whitepapers/specification
9              Test Data:      https://github.com/phuse-org/phuse-scripts/tree/master/data/adam/cdisc
10             Sample Output:
10       ! https://github.com/phuse-org/phuse-scripts/blob/master/whitepapers/WPCT/outputs_sas/WPCT-F.07.01_Box_plot_DIABP_by_visit_
10       ! for_timepoint_815.pdf
11         
12         	*Some changes*
13         	
14         	********************
15         	Comments and modifications 2020-01-17:
16         	
17         	- comment %assert_timepoint_exist as this is not available;
18         	
19         	To have this script runnable for the example data, you need to update some settings (SASAUTOS, pathes),
20         	furthermore you need to create dummy ATPTN and ATPT variables as these are currently not in the test data.
21         	
22         	OPTIONS SASAUTOS=("<PATH>/whitepapers/utilities", SASAUTOS);
23         	OPTIONS MRECALL MAUTOSOURCE;
24         	
25         	%let ds = ADLBC;
26         	%util_access_test_data(&ds);
27         	%* program requires time point variables, so create dummy content as not available in test data;
28         	DATA &ds;
29         		SET &ds;
30         		ATPTN = 1;
31         		ATPT = "TimePoint unknown";
32         	RUN;
33         	
34         	%let outputs_folder = <PATH>/results;
35         	********************
36         
37             Using this program:
38         
39               * See USER PROCESSING AND SETTINGS, below, to configure this program for your environment and data
40               * Program will plot all visits, ordered by AVISITN, with maximum of 20 boxes on a page (default)
41                 + see user option MAX_BOXES_PER_PAGE, below, to change limit of 20 boxes per page
42               * Program separately plots all parameters provided in PARAMCD
43               * Measurements within each PARAMCD and ATPTN determine precision of statistical results
44                 + MEAN gets 1 extra decimal, STD DEV gets 2 extra decimals
45                 + see macro UTIL_VALUE_FORMAT to modify this behavior
46               * If your treatment names are too long for the summary table, abbreviate them
47                 in the input data, and add a footnote that explains your short Tx codes
48                 + This program contains custom code to shorted Tx labels in the PhUSE CS test data
49                 + See "2b) USER SUBSET of data", below
50         
51             TO DO list for program:
52         
53               * Complete and confirm specifications (see Outliers & Reference limit discussions, below)
54                   https://github.com/phuse-org/phuse-scripts/tree/master/whitepapers/specification
                                                           The SAS System

55               * For annotated RED CIRCLEs outside normal range limits
56                   UPDATE the test data so that default outputs have some IQR OUTLIER SQUAREs that are not also RED.
57               * The footnote could dynamically describe any normal range lines that appear. See the Fig. 7.1 specifications.
58               * LABS & ECG - ADaM VS/LAB/ECG domains have some different variables and variable naming conventions.
59                   - What variables are used for LAB/ECG box plots?
60                   - What visits/time-points are relevant to LAB/ECG box plots?
61                   - Handle all of these within one template program?
62                     Or separate them (and accept some redundancy)?
63                   - NB: Currently vars like AVISIT, AVISITN, ATPT, ATPTN are hard-coded in this program
64         
65         end HEADER ***/
66         
67         
68         
69           /************************************
70            *** USER PROCESSING AND SETTINGS ***
71            ************************************
72         
73             1) REQUIRED - PhUSE CS Utilities macro library.
74                These templates require the PhUSE CS macro utilities:
75                  https://github.com/phuse-org/phuse-scripts/tree/master/whitepapers/utilities
76                User must ensure that SAS can find PhUSE CS macros in the SASAUTOS path (see EXECUTE ONE TIME, below)
77         
78             2) OPTIONAL - Subset measurement data, to limit resulting plots to specific
79                  - Parameters
80                  - Analysis Timepoints
81                  - Visits
82         
83             3) REQUIRED - Key user settings (libraries, data sets, variables and box plot options)
84                M_LB:   Libname containing ADaM measurement data, such as ADVS.
85                        WORK by default, since step (2) creates the desired WORK subset.
86                M_DS:   Measuments data set, such as ADVS.
87         
88                T_VAR:  Variable in M_DS with the Treatment Name, such as TRTP, TRTA.
89                TN_VAR: Variable in M_DS with the Treatment Number (display controls order), such as TRTPN, TRTAN.
90                M_VAR:  Variable in M_DS with measurements data, such as AVAL.
91                LO_VAR: Variable in M_DS with LOWER LIMIT of reference range, such as ANRLO.
92                        Required to highlight values outside reference range (RED DOT in box plot), and reference lines
93                HI_VAR: Variable in M_DS with UPPER LIMIT of reference range, such as ANRHI.
94                        Required to highlight values outside reference range (RED DOT in box plot), and reference lines
95         
96                P_FL:  Population flag variable. 'Y' indicates record is in population of interest.
97                A_FL:  Analysis Flag variable.   'Y' indicates that record is selected for analysis.
98         
99                REF_LINES:
100                     Option to specify which Normal Range reference lines to include in box plots
101                     <NONE | UNIFORM | NARROW | ALL | numeric-value(s)> See discussion in Central Tendency White Paper
102                     NONE    - No reference lines on box plot
103                     UNIFORM - Default. preferred alternative to default. Only plot LOW/HIGH ref lines if uniform for all obs
104                     NARROW  - Display only the narrow normal limits: max LOW, and min HIGH limits
105                     ALL     - Discouraged, since displaying ALL reference lines confuses review of data display
106                     numeric-values - space-delimited list of reference line values, such as a 0 reference line for displays of
106      ! change.
107        
108               MAX_BOXES_PER_PAGE:
109                     Maximum number of boxes to display per plot page (see "Notes", above)
110        
111               OUTPUTS_FOLDER:
                                                           The SAS System

112                     Location to write PDF outputs (WITHOUT final back- or forward-slash)
