44           /************************************
45            *** USER PROCESSING AND SETTINGS ***
46            ************************************
47         
48             1) REQUIRED - PhUSE CS Utilities macro library.
49                These templates require the PhUSE CS macro utilities:
50                  https://github.com/phuse-org/phuse-scripts/tree/master/whitepapers/utilities
51                User must ensure that SAS can find PhUSE CS macros in the SASAUTOS path (see EXECUTE ONE TIME, below)
52         
53             2) OPTIONAL - Subset measurement data, to limit resulting plots to specific
                                                           The SAS System

54                  - Parameters
55                  - Analysis Timepoints
56                  - Visits
57         
58             3) REQUIRED - Key user settings (libraries, data sets, variables and box plot options)
59                M_LB:   Libname containing ADaM measurement data, such as ADVS.
60                        WORK by default, since step (2) creates the desired WORK subset.
61                M_DS:   Measuments data set, such as ADVS.
62         
63                T_VAR:  Variable in M_DS with the Treatment Name, such as TRTP, TRTA.
64                TN_VAR: Variable in M_DS with the Treatment Number (display controls order), such as TRTPN, TRTAN.
65         
66                C_VAR:  Variable in M_DS with change-from-baseline data, such as CHG.
67         
68                B_VAR:    (Leave blank to omit p-value from summary table.) Variable in M_DS with baseline measurements
69                REF_TRTN: (Leave blank to omit p-value from summary table.) Numeric value of TN_VAR for reference (comparator)
69       ! treatment
70         
71                P_FL:  Population flag variable. 'Y' indicates record is in population of interest.
72                A_FL:  Analysis Flag variable.   'Y' indicates POST-BASELINE obs that contain:
73                         * A non-missing post-baseline measure   (either LAST, MIN or MAX measurement post-baseline)
74                         * including a non-missing baseline val  (LAST, MIN or MAX to match the post-baseline measurement)
75                         * and a non-missing chg from baseline   (based on the above baseline & post-baseline measurements)
76                       For an example, see the PhUSE CS derivation in ADaM/derive_lastminmax_measure.sas
77                       But then remove Baseline obs.
78         
79                C_MODE: Change Mode label. This is merely a label that describes the obs flagged by user-specified A_FL
80                         * LAST: Default. Change from LAST baseline to LAST post-baseline analysis measurement
81                         * MIN:  Change from MIN baseline to MIN post-baseline analysis measurement
82                         * MAX:  Change from MAX baseline to MAX post-baseline analysis measurement
83         
84                MAX_BOXES_PER_PAGE:
85                      Maximum number of boxes to display per plot page (see "Notes", above)
86         
87                OUTPUTS_FOLDER:
88                      Location to write PDF outputs (WITHOUT final back- or forward-slash)
89         
90           ************************************
91           *** user processing and settings ***
92           ************************************/
