1          /************************************************************************************************
2           REMOVE ENTIRELY DUPLICATED ROWS
                                                           The SAS System

3               This program sort the input table by all columns to ensure fully duplicated rows are
4                   adjacent. Then duplicate rows are removed from the output table.
5               Keywords: PROC SORT, remove duplicates
6               SAS Versions: SAS 9, SAS Viya
7               Documentation:
7        ! https://documentation.sas.com/?cdcId=pgmsascdc&cdcVersion=default&docsetId=proc&docsetTarget=p1nd17xr6wof4sn19zkmid81p926
7        ! .htm
8               1. Create the WORK.CLASSTEST table and print it.
9               2. PROC SORT sorts rows by all columns so that duplicated rows will be sequential.
10                 The NODUPKEY option deletes rows with duplicate BY values, thus eliminating entirely
11                 duplicated rows.
12         ************************************************************************************************/
13         
14         
15         data classtest;                                                       /*1*/
16            infile datalines dsd;
17            input
18               Name :$7.
19               Subject :$7.
20               Score;
21         datalines4;

